### Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@contentType = application/json

### 1. GET - Récupérer tous les utilisateurs
GET {{baseUrl}}/users
Accept: {{contentType}}

###

### 2. POST - Créer un nouvel utilisateur
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "username": "johndoe",
  "password": "securepassword123",
  "email": "john.doe@example.com",
  "firstName": "John",
  "lastName": "Doe",
  "birthDate": "1990-05-15",
  "role": "USER",
  "iban": "FR1420041010050500013M02606",
  "signinDate": "2024-01-15T10:30:00",
  "banned": false
}

###

### 3. POST - Créer un utilisateur ADMIN
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "username": "admin",
  "password": "adminpassword456",
  "email": "admin@company.com",
  "firstName": "Alice",
  "lastName": "Smith",
  "birthDate": "1985-12-01",
  "role": "ADMIN",
  "iban": "GB29NWBK60161331926819",
  "signinDate": "2024-01-10T08:00:00",
  "banned": false
}

###

### 4. GET - Récupérer un utilisateur par ID (remplacer {id} par un ID existant)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/1
Accept: {{contentType}}

###

### 5. GET - Récupérer un utilisateur par ID inexistant (devrait retourner 404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/999
Accept: {{contentType}}

###

### 6. PUT - Mettre à jour un utilisateur existant (remplacer {id} par un ID existant)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/users/1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "username": "johnupdated",
  "password": "newpassword789",
  "email": "john.updated@example.com",
  "firstName": "John",
  "lastName": "Updated",
  "birthDate": "1990-05-15",
  "role": "USER",
  "iban": "FR1420041010050500013M02606",
  "signinDate": "2024-01-15T10:30:00",
  "banned": false
}

###

### 7. PUT - Tentative de mise à jour d'un utilisateur inexistant (devrait retourner 404)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/users/999
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "username": "nonexistent",
  "password": "password123",
  "email": "nonexistent@example.com",
  "firstName": "Non",
  "lastName": "Existent",
  "birthDate": "1995-01-01",
  "role": "USER",
  "iban": "FR1420041010050500013M02606",
  "signinDate": "2024-01-01T12:00:00",
  "banned": false
}

###

### 8. DELETE - Supprimer un utilisateur par ID (remplacer {id} par un ID existant)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/users/2
Accept: {{contentType}}

###

### 9. DELETE - Tentative de suppression d'un utilisateur inexistant (devrait retourner 404)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/users/999
Accept: {{contentType}}

###

### 10. POST - Test de validation - utilisateur avec données invalides
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "username": "a",
  "password": "b",
  "email": "invalid-email",
  "firstName": "",
  "lastName": "D",
  "birthDate": "2030-01-01",
  "role": "INVALID_ROLE",
  "iban": "invalid-iban",
  "signinDate": "2030-01-01T12:00:00",
  "banned": false
}

###

### 11. POST - Test avec champs manquants
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "username": "incomplete",
  "email": "incomplete@example.com"
}

###

### 12. POST - Utilisateur avec date de naissance dans le futur (devrait échouer)
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "username": "futureuser",
  "password": "password123",
  "email": "future@example.com",
  "firstName": "Future",
  "lastName": "User",
  "birthDate": "2030-01-01",
  "role": "USER",
  "iban": "FR1420041010050500013M02606",
  "signinDate": "2024-01-15T10:30:00",
  "banned": false
}

###

### 13. POST - Utilisateur banni
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "username": "banneduser",
  "password": "password123",
  "email": "banned@example.com",
  "firstName": "Banned",
  "lastName": "User",
  "birthDate": "1988-03-10",
  "role": "USER",
  "iban": "DE89370400440532013000",
  "signinDate": "2024-01-01T09:00:00",
  "banned": true
}